      players: '4 players in two partnerships (partners sit opposite each other).',
      deck: 'Standard 52-card pack. Ranking: A (high), K, Q, J, 10, 9, 8, 7, 6, 5, 4, 3, 2 (low).',
      equipment: "Standard deck, paper and pen for tracking 'Kots'.",
      dealing: 'Dealer deals a batch of 5 cards to each player. After trump selection, the remaining cards are dealt in batches of 4. Play is anticlockwise.',
    },
    turnFlow: "1. Trump Selection: Usually 'First Unable to Follow Suit' (the first time a player can't follow, the card they play sets the trump suit) or 'Eldest Hand' choice.\n2. Double Sar Mechanic: Tricks are not picked up immediately. They accumulate in the center. A player must win two consecutive tricks to pick up the pile.\n3. Breaking the Sar: If the leads change between players of different teams, the pile grows until someone wins two in a row.\n4. Final Trick: The winner of the 13th trick picks up all remaining cards in the center, regardless of the consecutive win rule.",
